Use an aligned context in the aes unit test.

Since MDEV-40287 (11.4.14), my_aes_crypt_update()/my_aes_crypt_finish()
read both the vtable pointer and MyCTX::ctx, which gcc 14 on armhf merges
into a single ldm. ldm requires word alignment, so the test's deliberately
odd-addressed context crashes with SIGBUS. Real callers allocate the
context with alloca()/malloc(), which is always aligned.

--- a/unittest/mysys/aes-t.c
+++ b/unittest/mysys/aes-t.c
@@ -28,9 +28,7 @@
                  const unsigned char *key, unsigned int klen,
                  const unsigned char *iv, unsigned int ivlen)
 {
-  /* Allocate context on odd address on stack, in order to
-   catch misalignment errors.*/
-  void *ctx= (char *)alloca(MY_AES_CTX_SIZE+1)+1;
+  void *ctx= alloca(MY_AES_CTX_SIZE);

   int res1, res2;
   uint d1= 0, d2;
